  "steps": [
    "Real fourteen-module/thirty-capability HTTP editor mounts an independent authored-axis position alignment module. No object or reference is preselected; X is the only default. One object or a missing reference cannot enable Check or Apply. Native BOM/CRLF source includes escaped keys and literal Unicode/CRLF names. Old readonly preview draws actual WebGL2 with the software GPU recorded.",
    "Two explicitly selected stable UUIDs, including the hidden reference, align only authored X positions to the reference original coordinate. Complete before/after objects include the unchanged reference; net paths contain only the changed component. All other object fields, camera/light, BOM/CRLF and escaped-key spelling remain. Chinese/English/Japanese at 390px preserve filter, selection, reference, axis and approval; responsive comparison and reachable footer are asserted. Cancel leaves both source and disk untouched.",
    "Apply accepts the exact advanced owner receipt and updates unsaved source memory only; disk remains original until ordinary Save. Fresh readonly preview reflects the authored position change with actual readPixels. Save writes the exact reviewed candidate. Reopening reads persisted positions; repeating already-equal X alignment is a native no-op with no Apply approval.",
    "Author Y and Z component alignment are each separately reviewed, applied to memory and saved exactly, preserving other coordinates and UUIDs. Deselecting the reference clears it, and selecting that object again never chooses a replacement automatically. A separate unsaved 128-object scene explicitly selects every object and a hidden final reference, reviews all 128 declarations and cancels without writing disk. This operation does not align rotated edges, bounds or screen positions."
  ],
